From 5ff946df22a4aad9a8c29ed83e2b2e3c3f95df4f Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: A9 project <dmayala@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Thu, 15 Oct 2026 16:03:42 -0700
Subject: [PATCH] drm/a9_eink: render-ahead ring: a producer renders the
 update, the worker only composes and commits

Mainline Android runs 5-7 (8 CPUs, SCHED_FIFO worker): drive frames were
repeated (late_drive 11-12, max_gap_drive 23.7-25.5 ms) and in run 7 one was
held past the 35.3 ms frame-progress deadline (stall_fault, HV dropped). The
worker rendered every frame between its own blocking commits.

- New producer kthread "a9_eink_r" (nice -10) renders a REAL update's frames
  (init flash, if pending, then the update) into a ring of 32 slots, each
  byte 0 of the data region only (rows 5..828, words 0..411: 339,488 B;
  10.9 MB in all). a9r_pack refuses a frame with drive data outside the
  data region (never produced by the core).
- The worker (consumer) waits until the ring is full or the update is
  completely rendered, keeping the panel on idle (template) refreshes at
  the frame rate meanwhile (bounded, 2 s), then per frame does only the
  byte-0 compose into the template buffer (a9x_show_data: equal to
  a9x_compose of the full frame) and the commit.
- Underrun (ring empty before the producer is done): idle frame, update
  aborted (forced clear next), no fault latch: the frame-progress interlock
  still covers any drive frame held too long. enable=0, transport errors,
  prefill timeout: idle frame, producer stopped, abort. The worker holds
  eng_lock for the update and lends the engine to the producer until
  a9r_stop() returns.
- Dry runs (E5a) and zero_test keep the synchronous path; trace hashing
  moves to the producer (same frames).
- Pacing diagnosis in status line 4: commit_max_us / commit_slow (the DRM
  commit call itself > 1.5 periods), compose_max_us, render_max_us,
  prefill_us, ring_min, underruns: shows whether the msm commit is what
  takes more than a period.
Power path unchanged: same transport power-on/off, template, commit path,
interlock (armed/disarmed by the same a9x_commit_locked), caps and bins.
Host harness cases (17)-(22).

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
